{"title":"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A restaurant offers three desserts, and exactly twice as many appetizers as main courses. A dinner consists of an appetizer, a main course, and a dessert. What is the least number of main courses that a restaurant should offer so that a customer could have a different dinner each night in the year <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b910f4dafca80b54c6e7bedf63b6485eebff0764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afcf718ae50f3e8e247a7844d1c575f80b3a78c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 6 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 7 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of main courses the restaurant serves, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93d829d38f1f73cd97c8fd926e636e968d0c158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2m$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> is the number of appetizers. Then the number of dinner combinations is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/9/0895c012f89c177a5bfabcce51fba1908dc6274b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2m\\times m\\times3=6m^2$\" width=\"150\" height=\"15\" />. Since the customer wants to eat a different dinner in all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/988ab73be88b10c8cbf520db5e7cb4b3c6531963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$365$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> days of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b910f4dafca80b54c6e7bedf63b6485eebff0764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />, we must have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cf98d5671ee23f70e11b515cb3579ae29da7e0d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 6m^2 &amp;\\geq 365\\\\ m^2 &amp;\\geq 60.83\\ldots.\\end{align*}\" width=\"128\" height=\"45\" />\nAlso, year 2003 is not a leap year, because 2003 divided by 4 does not equal an integer.\nThe smallest integer value that satisfies this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d724db96e8cb75176d053467614c78aca041470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> denote the number of main courses needed to meet the requirement. Then the number of dinners available is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd8ed2c3cf98eb2c8fe311945d9caafad0e014d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot m \\cdot 2m = 6m^2$\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f521656db779d024e6aff0f9a3771ac28d2c3db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> must be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d4c51745a769b728eeeb13cc972b81ef1c2895a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$365/6 \\approx 61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/8854b24d936563212449c5e91f6abca432d7ac02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^2 = 49&lt;61&lt;64 = 8^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"183\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81ca9c5c8715be868438500743202d6773d05bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" /> main courses is enough, but 7 is not. The smallest integer value that satisfies this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d724db96e8cb75176d053467614c78aca041470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of main courses and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> be the number of appetizers.\nSince there are 3 desserts, the number of possible dinner choices would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b6a3acc889daf0086688d67ad35128d0c9572c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x \\cdot x \\cdot 3 = 6x^2$\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" /> for any number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Since a year has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/988ab73be88b10c8cbf520db5e7cb4b3c6531963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$365$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> days, we can assume that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a43f58bcf34b80c70d4cc58123fb53631e7bf024.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 6x^2 \\ge 365 \\end{align*}\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/6/1760065d5764f93c78aa2526ad30764b01513712.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x^2 \\ge 61 \\end{align*}\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/871e4878e2b7b504e2807aa5d46ca020410561a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x \\ge 7.8 \\end{align*}\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />\nThe least option that is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/6/a665e31452d1983d23dde37dc75ac4065541b0b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7.8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d724db96e8cb75176d053467614c78aca041470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~ Alfi06\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/-Yv2R46IO4E\">https://youtu.be/-Yv2R46IO4E</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B\">2003 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?tit